{
 "about": "The lint ratchet's baseline (scripts/lint.mjs, pnpm lint): Biome's violations per rule and file when the linter came in, which may only go down. A new or raised count fails, and so does a lowered one until this file is rewritten with node scripts/lint.mjs --write-baseline (the `off` reasons are kept). `off`: each rule biome.json turns off, with why its hits are the code's idiom rather than a defect.",
 "biome": "2.5.15",
 "off": {
  "lint/style/noNonNullAssertion": "About 3,500 `!` after a lookup the code has just checked (maps, regex groups, test values); the type checker's strict mode is the guard.",
  "lint/style/useTemplate": "Style only: short concatenations read as well as templates.",
  "lint/complexity/noCommaOperator": "The comma in an arrow body or a loop step is a deliberate short form (`() => (clearTimeout(t), r())`).",
  "lint/suspicious/noAssignInExpressions": "Deliberate idioms: `while ((m = re.exec(s)))`, `void (out += t)`, `(x ??= make()).use()`.",
  "lint/suspicious/noTemplateCurlyInString": "`${…}` inside plain strings is shell or scenario-template text on purpose (hooks, fake tools in tests).",
  "lint/suspicious/noControlCharactersInRegex": "The control-character patterns are the point: untrusted text is cleaned of them before it is shown.",
  "lint/suspicious/useIterableCallbackReturn": "`forEach((x) => set.add(x))` returns a value nobody reads; harmless.",
  "lint/suspicious/noThenProperty": "`then` is a domain word here (the scenario before an edit, `replanEdit({ now, then })`), never awaited.",
  "lint/correctness/noChildrenProp": "The Studio's tests and kit build elements with `createElement(C, { children })` on purpose.",
  "lint/correctness/noVoidTypeReturn": "`return v.forEach(walk)` in a void walker is a short form of a call and a return.",
  "lint/correctness/noEmptyCharacterClassInRegex": "`[^]` (any character, newlines included) is used on purpose in multi-line test patterns."
 },
